WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.100
Who's involved?

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.998
The platform and pipeline engineers
who own the scheduled checks,

3
00:00:04.998 --> 00:00:09.675
and the security officers and reviewers
who receive the evidence and verify it.

4
00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:11.912
The permissions are deliberately split.

5
00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:13.952
A handful of administrator roles,

6
00:00:13.952 --> 00:00:17.012
or the app's owner, can add
the federated credential.

7
00:00:17.012 --> 00:00:21.276
The pipeline's identity gets only
the read permissions its checks need,

8
00:00:21.276 --> 00:00:23.950
plus write access to
one evidence container.

9
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:28.888
And only the second job, which has no
Azure access at all, can write issues.

10
00:00:28.888 --> 00:00:32.760
No identity both reads the tenant
and writes to the tracker.
